 server←{which}Run port;folder;rc;msg
⍝ Start the Exercise 3 ticker service on localhost, and its broadcast loop
⍝ which  - [optional] 'Start' (default) or 'Solution': the folder whose code is loaded
⍝ port   - the port to listen on (the README uses 8083)
⍝ server - the Jarvis server; stop it and the broadcast loop with Stop
⍝          ⍬ if Setup has not been run or the folder does not exist
⍝          the Jarvis server, not started, if it could not start (e.g. the port is in use)
⍝ The code is loaded into #.Ex3: Ticker (called when a browser connects) and Broadcast (the loop).
⍝ Edit with )ED, e.g. )ED #.Ex3.Ticker; the server uses the change straight away. The running Broadcast loop
⍝ keeps its old code, so after editing Broadcast, run Restart. (Running Run again would reload the code from the
⍝ files and throw your edits away.)
⍝ The web page is served from html/index.html. Run also loads the supplied Stop and Restart.
⍝ Usage:
⍝      server←Run 8083
⍝      server←'Solution' Run 8083
 server←⍬
 :If 0=⎕NC'which'
     which←'Start'
 :EndIf
 :If 0=#.⎕NC'WorkshopRoot'
     ⎕←'Problem: run Setup first (see Exercises/README.md)'
     →0
 :EndIf
 folder←#.WorkshopRoot,'/Exercises/Ex3-SSE/'
 :If ~⎕NEXISTS folder,which
     ⎕←'Problem: no folder "',folder,which,'"; use ''Start'' or ''Solution'''
     →0
 :EndIf

⍝ Stop the server and loop from an earlier Run, if they are still running.
⍝ On Linux, a second server on a port already used in the same session starts without an error, and the old one
⍝ keeps answering with the old code. On Windows the second server fails to start with "port in use". Either way, stop first.
 {}{2 #.⎕FIX'file://',folder,⍵}¨'Stop.aplf' 'Restart.aplf'
 :If 9=⌊#.⎕NC'Ex3Server'
 :AndIf #.Ex3Server.Running
     #.Stop
 :EndIf

⍝ Load the functions into a fresh #.Ex3, and set up the data the loop uses
 #.⎕EX'Ex3'
 'Ex3'#.⎕NS''
 {}{2 #.Ex3.⎕FIX'file://',⍵}¨⊃0(⎕NINFO⍠1)folder,which,'/*.aplf'
 #.Ex3.Symbols←'ALPHA' 'IOTA' 'OMEGA' 'RHO'
 #.Ex3.Prices←120 85.5 64 210.25
 #.Ex3.Headlines←'IOTA counts on strong demand' 'RHO reshapes its portfolio' 'ALPHA leads the market from the left' 'OMEGA has the last word' 'Analysts reduce their outlook, then scan it again'
 #.Ex3.Running←1 ⍝ Broadcast loops while this is 1; Stop sets it to 0

 server←#.Jarvis.New''
 #.Ex3Server←server
 server.Port←port
 server.CodeLocation←#.Ex3
 server.SSEEndpoints←'Ticker'     ⍝ GET /Ticker opens an event stream; Jarvis calls Ticker when a client connects
 server.IncludeFns←'Ticker'       ⍝ no ordinary endpoints: Broadcast must not be callable over HTTP
 server.HTMLInterface←folder,'html' ⍝ serve the web page from html/
 server.DYALOG_JARVIS_THREAD←'DEBUG' ⍝ run in the background, keep the session usable
 (rc msg)←server.Start
 :If rc≠0
     ⎕←'Problem: could not start the server: ',msg
     ⎕←'If port ',(⍕port),' is in use, try another, for example: server←Run ',⍕port+10
     →0
 :EndIf
 #.Ex3Thread←#.Ex3.Broadcast&server ⍝ the broadcast loop runs in its own thread
 ⎕←'Exercise 3 (',which,') is running: open http://localhost:',(⍕port),' in your browser'
